.TH ZORG 1 2026-10-05 "zorg 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zorg \- a fast, lightweight, CLI-only Zcash wallet
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zorg
.RI [ GLOBAL\ FLAGS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zorg
is a command-line Zcash wallet. It manages accounts, keeps a local
copy of the shielded blockchain state in a SQLite database, and builds
and broadcasts shielded transfers natively from the terminal. The
mnemonic is stored in the macOS Keychain; wallet state lives in a
SQLite database. zorg_index.db and new databases live in
.IR ~/Library/Application\ Support/zorg/ .
zorg_index.db is the record of which accounts exist: each account's name,
network, and database path. It also holds the settings: the account the app
opens, whether it hides balances, and a server for testnet and for mainnet
that every command uses unless
.B --lwd
is given. Each account has its own database, and each account's phrase is
stored in Keychain.
The database itself is not encrypted.
Running zorg without a command in a terminal shows the default account's
balance, syncing in the background, with a menu to send, receive, or see
history,
.B s
for settings, until
.B q
or Esc quits; with no accounts it offers to create an
account or import a recovery phrase. Outside a terminal it lists accounts.
Names are case-sensitive and unique.
An account whose database is missing is reported as unavailable until
.B zorg delete
removes it.
.SH GLOBAL FLAGS
Recognized before or after the command:
.TP
.BI \-\-network " main|test|regtest"
The new account's network, for create and import only. Defaults to mainnet.
.TP
.BI \-\-lwd " url"
lightwalletd endpoint override. Well-known public endpoints are the
default; use only if you need a specific one.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-V\fR, \fB\-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI zorg\ create " [name]"
Create a new seed database and print its mnemonic. Ask for a name if omitted. The wallet birthday is the current chain tip (resolved via
the lightwalletd endpoint) minus 100, rounded down to a multiple of 100,
and is printed with the address.
.TP
.BI zorg\ import " [name] [\-\-birthday\ height]"
Import a phrase at derivation index 0 into a new database. Ask for a name if
omitted. Reject a phrase already known on the same network. Higher
account-index discovery is not implemented.
.TP
.B zorg\ accounts
List all accounts across known databases. Each line shows the account
name, network, and unified address.
.TP
.BI zorg\ balance " [\-\-account\ name]"
Print spendable, pending, and locked balances for the account
(the only account, if none given; otherwise a name is required).
.TP
.BI zorg\ address " [\-\-new] [\-\-account\ name]"
Print the account's most recently used unified receiving address.
After restoring an account from its recovery phrase, this can be an address
that has already been paid; make a new one before handing it out.
With
.BR \-\-new ,
make a new address for the account and print it; the account must have been
synced first.
Every address the account has made keeps receiving.
.TP
.BI zorg\ sync " [\-\-account\ name]"
Sync every known database once, or the chosen account's database.
.TP
.BI zorg\ status " [\-\-account\ name]"
Print scan progress for every known database, or the chosen account's database.
.TP
.BI zorg\ send " to\ amount [\-\-memo\ text] [\-\-account\ name]"
Propose, authorize, and broadcast a shielded transfer of
.I amount
(ZEC on mainnet, TAZ on testnet)
to
.IR to .
Prints the fee before authorization and the broadcast txids after.
.TP
.BI zorg\ history " [\-\-account\ name] [\-\-limit\ n]"
Print recent transactions.
.TP
.BI zorg\ tx " txid [\-\-account\ name]"
Print one transaction of the account in full: its amount and status, the
addresses it involves, its pool, fee, and memo.
.I txid
is written as
.B zorg history
and block explorers show it.
.TP
.BI zorg\ recovery " [\-\-account\ name]"
Print the account's recovery phrase and wallet birthday. Reading the
phrase from the macOS Keychain asks for Touch ID or the login password.
.TP
.BI zorg\ validate " address"
Check whether
.I address
is a valid Zcash address.
.TP
.BI zorg\ delete " \-\-account\ name"
Delete an account and its Keychain entry after a warning, Enter, and Touch ID
or the login password. Deleting an account deletes its database.
